RoboLab — Full Product Requirements Document (PRD)

Advanced Mobile Robotics Engineering & Simulation Platform

Version: 1.0
Product type: Native Android application
Working name: RoboLab
Primary objective: Build a premium, interactive, zero-cost virtual robotics laboratory that enables users to design, program, simulate, and debug robots on Android devices.

---

1. Product Vision

RoboLab is a mobile-first robotics engineering platform that transforms an Android phone into a virtual robotics workshop.

Users should be able to construct robots from individual components, configure their mechanical properties, program their behavior, run physics-based simulations, observe sensor outputs, and diagnose failures without purchasing physical robotics hardware.

The product must combine the visual quality of a modern 3D application with the practical functionality of an engineering tool.

RoboLab must not be merely a 3D viewer, a static robot gallery, a collection of educational articles, or a chatbot.

Core product promise: Build it. Program it. Simulate it. Break it. Improve it.

1.1 Product principles

1. Visual quality must be premium, polished, and consistent.
2. Every primary interface must perform a real function.
3. Simulations must use actual implemented calculations rather than fabricated results.
4. Projects must persist across app restarts.
5. The app must remain usable on mid-range Android devices.
6. Core functionality must work offline.
7. The MVP must not depend on paid AI APIs or subscriptions.
8. Advanced features must be introduced incrementally without destabilizing completed functionality.

