13. Project Management and Persistence

Project persistence is mandatory.

13.1 Project data

A saved project must include:

- Project identifier.
- Name and description.
- Project format version.
- Robot components.
- Component properties.
- Component relationships.
- Joint configurations.
- Sensor configurations.
- Controller assignments.
- Program data.
- Environment settings.
- Relevant simulation settings.
- Creation and modification timestamps.

13.2 Save and recovery

Implement:

- Explicit save.
- Autosave with safe timing.
- Save status indicator.
- Unsaved-change warnings.
- Project duplication.
- Rename.
- Delete with confirmation.
- Project restoration after application restart.
- Handling of invalid or outdated project files.
- Schema migration when formats change.

Use a versioned project format and safe writes. Corrupting one project must not corrupt every saved project.

13.3 Import and export

Provide a documented native RoboLab project format.

Later releases may support compatible robot description formats, such as a carefully scoped URDF importer/exporter.

Import support must validate files and report unsupported elements instead of silently discarding them.

