17. Security and Stability

- Validate imported project files.
- Avoid arbitrary execution of untrusted code.
- Limit program execution and support cancellation.
- Handle malformed project data safely.
- Request only necessary Android permissions.
- Do not request Accessibility permissions or unrelated sensitive permissions.
- Do not collect unnecessary personal information.
- Keep user projects local by default.
- Handle low-memory conditions gracefully.
- Provide meaningful error messages instead of blank screens.

If future text scripting is introduced, it must use a controlled runtime with a documented API rather than unrestricted access to the Android system.

