21. MVP Definition

The MVP is not a collection of attractive mockups.

It must contain one complete, working robotics workflow:

1. Open RoboLab.
2. Create a robot project.
3. Assemble a differential-drive robot.
4. Configure the wheels and distance sensor.
5. Place the robot in a test environment.
6. Run the simulation.
7. Observe real movement and sensor measurements.
8. Program basic obstacle avoidance using visual blocks.
9. Execute the program.
10. Save the project.
11. Restart the application.
12. Reopen the project and continue working.

If this workflow does not work, the MVP is not complete, regardless of how polished the screenshots look.

