22. Acceptance Criteria

A release candidate is acceptable only when:

- The Android application builds through the chosen cloud-build workflow.
- The main screens navigate correctly.
- The 3D viewport is interactive.
- Components can be added and configured.
- The robot hierarchy is persisted.
- Supported physics simulations run correctly.
- The distance sensor produces actual measurements.
- Visual programs affect the robot.
- Invalid assemblies and programs generate useful errors.
- Projects survive application restarts.
- Simulation execution can be stopped safely.
- Graphics settings affect real rendering behavior.
- Offline core functionality works.
- No primary action is a dead button.
- No simulated metric is fabricated merely to populate a dashboard.
- The app has been tested on a physical Android device.

