24. Definition of Success

RoboLab succeeds when users can do meaningful robotics work on an Android phone, rather than merely viewing a beautiful interface.

The long-term vision is a mobile robotics laboratory with increasingly sophisticated robot construction, simulation, programming, sensing, and control.

The immediate objective is narrower and measurable: deliver a polished Android application with a functional 3D workshop and one genuinely working, programmable simulated robot.

Build a reliable engineering foundation first. Expand toward the full vision without compromising correctness, usability, or the zero-budget constraint.